==Trivia==
*With each progressing form, this unit loses a wheel.
*The term [[wikipedia:Chopper (motorcycle)|chopper]] in Biker Cat's English description refers to a kind of motorcycle.
*In [[Battle Cats (Removed Game)|Battle Cats]], Tricycle Cat was inaccurately named "Bicycle-Cat". Its description also claimed that it was a regular participant of the [[wikipedia:Tour de France|Tour de France]].
*Tricycle Cat and Biker Cat have a number of [[Unimplemented Features|unused sprites]] within their spritesheets.
**Tricycle Cat has an unused black and white version of the rocket it fires in its attack.
**Biker Cat has both of the rockets from its prior form's spritesheet, but also a significantly larger missile. It also has a red version of the spikes it uses in its attack.
*[[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Wolf]] and Tricycle Cat are tied for the highest amount of [[Cat Combo]]s in the game at 8.
*In The Battle Cats Unite!, its True Form works properly but can only only obtained via save file editing.
*Prior to [[Version 15.6 Update|Version 15.6]], Tricycle Cat's descriptions read as follows:
<pre>Tricycle Cat
The coolest Cat on the block. (Area Attack)
Can't ride a real bike - parents said no.</pre>
<pre>Biker Cat
Born to be wild! (Area Attack)
Moved out and finally got his motorcycle!</pre>
<pre>Unicycle Cat
Was forced to scale down the number of wheels
thanks to a recession, but still stays positive.
Attacks groups of enemies (Area attack).</pre>
**Biker Cat's description referenced ''[[wikipedia:Born to Be Wild|Born to Be Wild]]'' by [[wikipedia:Steppenwolf|Steppenwolf]].
